{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"source_routes\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0241\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Association of Helicobacter pylori infection with survival outcomes in advanced gastric cancer patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供晚期胃癌中幽门螺杆菌活性感染与 ICI 疗效负相关的临床数据（DCR 47.1% vs 72.1%），支持特定病原体抑制免疫治疗响应的观点。其单中心回顾性设计及未校正 PD-L1 等混杂因素的局限，可用于讨论消化道肿瘤中微生物标志物的特异性及观察性研究的证据等级。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0242\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Targeting PD-L2/RGMb overcomes microbiome-related immunotherapy resistance\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"揭示微生物群通过下调树突状细胞 PD-L2 表达、解除 RGMb 对 CD8+ T 细胞抑制的具体分子机制，并鉴定出 C. cateniformis 为关键菌种。该研究在小鼠模型中验证了靶向 PD-L2/RGMb 轴可克服微生物介导的耐药，为联合治疗策略提供临床前依据，但需注明其肿瘤类型特异性限制。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0243\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"371 The association of the gut microbiota and clinical response to immune checkpoint inhibitors in patients with advanced cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供小样本队列中肠道微生物α多样性与临床获益相关的初步数据，并提出高多样性伴随 Treg 减少的免疫表型假设。由于生存分析未达统计学显著性且缺乏多变量校正，该材料适合作为讨论微生物多样性作为预测因子的争议性及小样本研究局限性的案例。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"805 Safety and emerging evidence of immune modulation of the live biotherapeutic MRx0518 in the neoadjuvant setting for patients awaiting surgical removal of solid tumours\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"报告活体生物制剂 MRx0518 在实体瘤患者新辅助治疗中的初步安全性及肿瘤组织免疫基因表达变化，显示其可能通过上调 NK/T 细胞相关通路发挥免疫调节作用。作为早期临床转化案例，它展示了 LBP 单药诱导免疫微环境改变的潜力，但需强调其尚未验证与 ICI 联用的临床疗效。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0245\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint blockade resistance in lung cancer: emerging mechanisms and therapeutic opportunities\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"将肠道微生物组置于肺癌 ICI 耐药的微环境因素框架中，指出其与肿瘤内在机制及缺氧等压力协同作用导致免疫抑制。作为综述性材料，它提供了微生物组作为非肿瘤细胞因素参与耐药的整体视角，支持多因素交互作用模型，但缺乏具体菌种或分子通路的原始数据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0246\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Five-year survival outcomes in NSCLC patients with concurrent GERD on proton pump inhibitors receiving pembrolizumab or nivolumab: A global study.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"基于大规模真实世界数据，证实 PPI 使用与 NSCLC 患者 ICI 治疗后 5 年生存率显著下降相关（37.2% vs 28.3%）。文中引用的机制假说（PPI 致菌群失调、有益菌减少）连接了药物干扰与临床结局，适合作为讨论外源性药物通过微生物组修饰 ICI 疗效的情境因素证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0247\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Friends close, enemies closer: the complex role of the microbiome in antitumor immunity\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统拆解微生物组调节免疫的三大机制（代谢物、抗原模拟、局部定植），并强调同一菌属（如乳酸杆菌）在不同癌种中效应的双向性。该综述为解释临床结果异质性提供了理论框架，并指出测序技术与空间成像等方法学挑战，适合用于讨论机制复杂性与标准化需求。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0248\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A Literature Review on the Impact of the Gut Microbiome on Cancer Treatment Efficacy, Disease Evolution and Toxicity: The Implications for Hematological Malignancies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦血液肿瘤，但提供了 SCFA 产生、Treg/Th17 调节等通用免疫机制及特定菌属（双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）的作用描述。可作为背景材料补充微生物 - 免疫互作的基础生物学原理，但在引用至实体瘤时需明确其来源背景，避免直接外推临床疗效结论。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0249\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 3523: A Black Raspberry dietary intervention to modify the gut microbiome and improve the response to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示黑覆盆子饮食干预在人体中未显著改变标志菌但在人源化小鼠模型中增强 ICI 疗效的“解耦”现象。该研究突出了饮食干预的复杂性及动物模型验证的重要性，适合作为讨论非药物干预策略潜力及其转化挑战（如人体菌群变化与功能输出不一致）的案例。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Exploring the role of the gut microbiome in modulating response to anti-PD-1 immunotherapy in melanoma patients\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"综合黑色素瘤中微生物组组成、代谢物与 T 细胞活化关联的证据，总结 FMT、饮食及益生菌干预的早期临床进展与风险。作为领域综述，它提供了构建“菌群 - 免疫 - 疗效”理论框架的素材，但需注明其结论主要基于黑色素瘤数据，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbial mechanisms to improve immune checkpoint blockade responsiveness\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"详细列举关键效应分子（如 cdAMP、肌苷、SagA）及其宿主受体（STING、A2AR、NOD2）介导的信号通路，区分了代谢物与蛋白抗原的不同作用模式。该材料是解析微生物调节 ICI 疗效分子机制的核心参考，并对比了生态疗法与还原论策略的优劣，适合机制章节深度展开。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0252\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Influence of Diet and Probiotics on the Response of Solid Tumours to Immunotherapy: Present and Future Perspectives\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"分类梳理地中海饮食、素食、Omega-3 等膳食因素及益生菌对微生物组和 ICI 响应的潜在影响，提出“饮食 - 菌群 - 免疫”的调节框架。作为高层级综述，它提供了非药物干预的分类清单和概念模型，但缺乏具体分子机制细节和定量疗效数据，适合背景介绍。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0253\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Role of gut microbiome on immunotherapy efficacy in melanoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"列出黑色素瘤中响应者富集的具体菌属（双歧杆菌、粪杆菌等）及非响应者特征，并概述抗生素破坏菌群导致免疫抑制的机制。该综述提供了特定 taxa 列表和 FMT 恢复敏感性的概念验证，同时指出临床数据有限和标准化缺失的挑战，适合用于临床关联与方法学讨论。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0254\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Obesity, cancer, and response to immune checkpoint inhibitors: Could the gut microbiota be the mechanistic link?\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"探讨“肥胖悖论”中微生物组作为潜在机械连接的作用，总结 BMI 与 ICI 生存获益的关联及 SCFA/瘦素介导的免疫调节假说。文中指出肥胖相关菌群与 ICI 响应菌群的重叠与分歧，适合用于讨论宿主代谢状态、饮食背景对微生物组效应的情境修饰作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0255\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"[Tracking Research Progress in the Modulatory Role of Gut Microbiome in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors Applied in Cancer Treatment].\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"结构化总结不同 ICI 类型（PD-1 vs CTLA-4）对应的特异性菌群特征及肌苷、STING 等潜在机制，并列出正在进行的 FMT/益生菌临床试验。该材料提供了药物类型特异性的菌群 - 效应对应表，适合用于比较不同检查点抑制剂受微生物调节的差异及转化现状。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0256\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Utilisation of Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Triple-Negative Breast Cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"确立三阴性乳腺癌中 ICI 治疗的临床基线及疗效异质性现状，指出存在阴性结局需探索调节因素。虽未直接涉及微生物组，但可作为背景材料界定特定实体瘤亚型的临床需求，为引入微生物组作为解释疗效差异的变量提供临床问题框架。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0257\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota reshaping the pancreatic cancer immune microenvironment: new avenues for immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦胰腺癌“冷肿瘤”特征，详述微生物群通过 TLR 信号、SCFA 及 TMAO 重编程巨噬细胞/T 细胞的具体机制，并提及万古霉素联合 ICI 失败的临床案例。该材料提供了肿瘤特异性微环境重塑的深层机制及干预反例，适合讨论机制复杂性与精准干预的必要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0258\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Effect of gut microbiota on immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) based cancer immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"归纳分子模拟、DC 激活及代谢物信号三大核心机制，并列出响应/耐药相关的具体细菌分类群。作为基础综述，它提供了生物学合理性框架和关键 taxa 列表，同时强调个体差异和研究间矛盾，适合用于构建理论模型和讨论证据不一致的原因。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0259\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Grade 3 and Grade 4 Cutaneous toxicities in patients across multiple solid tumour types receiving checkpoint inhibitor therapy: An observational study. The experience of a single large specialist institution.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供实体瘤 ICI 治疗中严重皮肤毒性（G3/4）的发生率及导致治疗中断的真实世界数据。虽未涉及微生物机制，但确立了毒性限制疗效的临床背景，可用于讨论 irAEs 管理对治疗持续性的影响，以及未来研究微生物组是否通过调节毒性间接影响生存的路径。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0260\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Evolving Landscape of Immunotoxicity: Charting Mechanisms and Future Strategies for Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Adverse Events\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"指出阿克曼氏菌等特定菌群在增强 ICI 疗效的同时可能增加 irAEs 风险的“双刃剑”效应，并提及 Th17/Treg 平衡的调节机制。该材料适合用于讨论疗效与毒性的权衡，以及微生物组干预在优化治疗窗口中的潜在挑战，强调共同机制下的不同临床结局。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions in Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"评估 FMT、定义菌群 consortia 等干预策略的早期临床结果及安全性，详述直接 T 细胞刺激、分子模拟和代谢物介导三大机制类别。该综述连接了基础机制与临床转化，提供了试验现状清单和方法学异质性分析，适合用于干预章节的现状评估与未来方向建议。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0262\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The role of the bacterial microbiome in the treatment of cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出代谢、免疫反应和细菌易位三大机制框架，列举阿克曼氏菌等关键标志物及抗生素负面影响的证据。作为广泛综述，它提供了跨癌种的背景知识和干预手段（FMT、饮食）概览，适合用于构建基础理论框架，但需注明部分机制主要源于动物模型。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0263\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Latest evidence on clinical outcomes and prognostic factors of advanced urothelial carcinoma in the era of immune checkpoint inhibitors: a narrative review.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总尿路上皮癌中伴随用药（抗生素、PPIs）通过改变菌群负向影响 ICI 疗效的临床证据，并提及益生菌 CBM588 的初步试验数据。该材料提供了特定癌种下药物 - 菌群互作的临床实例及干预尝试，适合讨论外源性因素修饰疗效的情境及早期转化探索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0264\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Systematic evaluation of immune regulation and modulation\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"强调微生物组作为免疫调节必要条件的生物学基础，指出当前证据多来自动物模型的局限，并提出多组学整合分析框架。该材料适合用于方法论章节，讨论样本采集、测序标准化及数据整合的重要性，为解释临床证据不足提供方法学背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0265\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Challenge for Development of Valuable Immuno-Oncology Biomarkers\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供黑色素瘤中菌群多样性与响应相关的早期证据，同时指出头颈癌唾液样本中未发现类似关联，强调肿瘤类型和采样部位的特异性。该材料适合用于讨论生物标志物开发的挑战，特别是单一标志物的局限性和多组学整合的必要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0266\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Antibiotics impair immune checkpoint inhibitor effectiveness in Hispanic patients with non‐small cell lung cancer (AB‐CLICaP)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在拉丁美洲 NSCLC 人群中证实抗生素暴露显著降低 OS 但不影响 PFS，提示地域人群特异性及统计效能差异。该研究提供了抗生素负面效应的特定人群证据，适合用于讨论抗生素使用时机、类型及人群背景对 ICI 疗效影响的异质性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0267\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immune‐related adverse events of antibody‐based biological medicines in cancer therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"确认微生物组在 ICI 疗效和结肠炎等 irAEs 中的双重作用，列举关键菌属及 FMT 应用案例，并阐述分子模拟和先天免疫激活机制。该综述提供了疗效与毒性关联的综合视角，适合讨论微生物组调节的复杂性及 FMT 在难治性病例中的潜力。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0268\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Molecular studies on the impact of microbiome on anticancer drug resistance\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述代谢物（SCFA、琥珀酸）介导的免疫调节及肠道 - 肿瘤易位轴机制，指出菌群效应的语境依赖性（宿主状态、饮食）。该材料提供了从分子通路到临床干预（FMT、纳米技术）的全面框架，适合深入解析耐药机制及讨论干预策略的局限性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0269\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"'Know thyself' – host factors influencing cancer response to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"将微生物组置于宿主因素（遗传、表型、用药）网络中，列出候选 taxa 及代谢物、先天免疫受体激活等机制，强调研究间不一致性及标准化需求。该综述适合用于讨论多因素交互作用模型，解释为何单一微生物标志物难以普适，并提出未来研究方向。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0270\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Composition of gastrointestinal microbiota in association with treatment response in individuals with metastatic castrate resistant prostate cancer progressing on enzalutamide and initiating treatment with anti-PD-1 (pembrolizumab)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在 mCRPC 队列中发现阿克曼氏菌与疗效负相关及通用预测指数失效的反例，提示既往内分泌治疗史和癌种特异性对菌群 - 疗效关系的修饰。该材料适合用于挑战通用生物标志物假设，讨论治疗史作为关键情境因素及机制的复杂性（如肌苷的双重作用）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0271\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The role of the gut microbiome on the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in Japanese responder patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在日本 NSCLC 小样本队列中报告特定菌属（乳杆菌、梭菌）与疗效的正向趋势及 Bilophila 的负向关联，尽管部分未达统计显著。该材料提供了亚洲人群的特异性数据，适合用于讨论种族/地域差异对微生物标志物的影响及小样本探索性研究的局限性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0272\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Combined or Sequential Treatment with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors and Car-T Cell Therapies for the Management of Haematological Malignancies: A Systematic Review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦血液肿瘤，但提供了 ICI 与 CAR-T 联用未普遍增效的对比证据，提示肿瘤微环境和治疗类型的特异性。可作为背景材料讨论 ICI 疗效的情境依赖性，说明除微生物组外，肿瘤类型和联合策略也是决定疗效的关键变量，避免过度泛化 ICI 增效机制。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0273\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Gut Microbiome and Cancer Immunotherapy: Can We Use the Gut Microbiome as a Predictive Biomarker for Clinical Response in Cancer Immunotherapy?\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"汇总多项临床研究中基线菌群（粪杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）与 ICI 响应的关联，重点报道 FMT 恢复难治患者响应的早期临床证据及抗生素负面影响。该综述提供了从观察到干预的证据链，适合用于评估生物标志物潜力和 FMT 转化前景，同时指出方法学异质性挑战。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0274\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome and cancer: mechanistic insights, diagnostic potential, and therapeutic strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统阐述抗原呈递、T 细胞启动、代谢物调节及抗原模拟四大核心机制，并提供 FMT 早期临床结果。该综述提供了详尽的机制分类和干预策略评估，适合用于构建机制章节的理论框架，同时强调情境依赖性和转化挑战，避免过度简化因果关系。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0275\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The association between antibiotic use and outcomes of HCC patients treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供 HCC 患者中抗生素使用未显著影响 ICI 疗效的阴性结果，提出肝硬化背景下的基线免疫抑制和特定菌群构成可能抵消抗生素负面效应的假说。该材料作为反例，适合用于讨论肿瘤类型特异性及宿主基础疾病对微生物 - 药物互作的修饰作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0276\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Tarloxotinib targets tumor hypoxia to improve therapeutic efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibition in a TLR9 dependent manner\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"展示靶向缺氧药物通过 TLR9 依赖途径激活先天免疫、重塑 TME 从而增强 ICI 疗效的机制，虽非直接微生物机制，但提供了 TME 物理化学性质调节免疫的平行案例。适合用于对比不同增敏策略（缺氧调节 vs 菌群调节）的异同及先天免疫信号的重要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0277\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Impact of influenza vaccination on survival of patients with advanced cancer receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (INVIDIa-2): final results of the multicentre, prospective, observational study\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供流感疫苗接种与部分实体瘤患者 ICI 生存获益相关的观察性证据，提出“旁观者效应”和免疫超激活假说。该材料适合用于讨论非微生物类外部免疫刺激对 ICI 疗效的潜在调节，作为系统性免疫激活机制的参照，并强调肿瘤类型异质性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0278\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitor-associated gastrointestinal adverse events in patients with colorectal cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"报告 MSI-H 结直肠癌患者中 ICI 相关结肠炎的低发生率及严重程度，并构建“肿瘤微环境 - 微生物组 - 免疫疗效/毒性”的理论框架。该材料提供了特定癌种的毒性基线数据，适合用于讨论微生物组在调节 irAEs 风险中的潜在作用及肿瘤生物学特征的影响。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0279\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome-selective DNA Pol IIIC inhibitors in oncology infection management\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"介绍 DNA Pol IIIC 抑制剂作为保留微生物多样性的新型抗生素类别，对比传统广谱抗生素的菌群破坏效应。该材料适合用于讨论抗生素选择策略对 ICI 疗效的潜在影响，提出“微生物组保护性”抗感染治疗作为未来优化 ICI 疗效的干预方向。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0280\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Insights into the Relationship Between the Gut Microbiome and Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Solid Tumors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"绘制跨癌种微生物标志物图谱，总结 SCFA 介导的表观遗传调节及代谢物诱导 T 细胞激活等机制，并强调地理、饮食等混杂因素。该综述提供了领域全景图，适合用于建立一致性/不一致性证据框架，并讨论标准化和未来多中心研究的必要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0281\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Oral–Gut Microbiome–Brain Axis in Cognition\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究聚焦神经退行性疾病与认知功能，虽涉及肠道菌群和 SCFA 的一般免疫调节功能，但缺乏肿瘤微环境、T 细胞浸润或 ICI 耐药的具体机制与临床数据，与实体瘤 ICI 疗效主题相关性极低，故不纳入。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0282\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Impact of Gut Microbiota-Derived Metabolites on the Tumor Immune Microenvironment\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"深入解析微生物代谢物（肌苷、SCFA、色氨酸衍生物）通过特定受体（A2A、AhR）和通路（mTOR、HDAC）直接调节 T 细胞和巨噬细胞功能的分子机制。该材料适合用于机制章节的核心部分，区分代谢物依赖与非依赖途径，并讨论肿瘤内微生物组的潜在作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0283\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome and serum short-chain fatty acids are associated with responses to chemo- or targeted therapies in Chinese patients with lung cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在非 ICI 治疗（化疗/靶向）背景下，发现特定菌群和异丁酸与肺癌治疗响应相关，揭示 GPCR-HAT-组蛋白乙酰化轴机制。该材料适合用于对比不同治疗模式下微生物作用的异同，扩展微生物调节抗癌疗效的普遍性视角，但需注意治疗机制差异。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0284\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Metagenomics and culturomics reveal the dual role of the gut microbiome in the development of immune-related toxicities and the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"揭示单一菌种（Paraclostridium bifermentans）通过活菌破坏屏障致毒、代谢物增强疗效的“双重角色”机制，并结合培养组学验证功能。该材料提供了机制复杂性的极致案例，适合讨论毒性 - 疗效权衡及培养组学在功能验证中的独特价值。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0285\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Breakthroughs in immune checkpoint therapy: overcoming NSCLC immune checkpoint therapy resistance with novel techniques\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述 NSCLC 中 ICI 耐药机制，特别提及 SCFA 增强疗效及 PD-L2-RGMB 轴等微生物相关路径。作为领域综述，它提供了 TME 重塑和克服耐药的综合视角，适合用于背景介绍和机制假设生成，但需结合原始研究验证具体通路。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0286\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immunological Drug–Drug Interactions in Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy: Mechanisms, Clinical Evidence, and Artificial Intelligence\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统阐述抗生素和 PPIs 通过破坏菌群多样性、减少有益菌从而削弱 DC 激活和 T 细胞功能的 iDDI 机制，并汇总时间窗敏感性证据。该材料适合用于讨论药物 - 微生物互作的情境因素，强调用药时机和种类对 ICI 疗效的关键影响。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0287\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Bacteria in cancer therapy: A new generation of weapons\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述外源性细菌疗法（如双歧杆菌、工程菌）通过 TLR/STING 通路激活免疫、下调 PD-L1 的机制，并提及 FMT 和活菌制剂临床试验。该材料适合用于讨论细菌介导免疫调节的广泛机制及治疗性细菌应用的潜力，需区分治疗菌与自然共生菌。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0288\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Impact of Patient Characteristics on the Outcomes of Patients with Gastrointestinal Cancers Treated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在胃肠道肿瘤中确认特定菌群（毛螺菌科、双歧杆菌）与 ICI 响应的关联，并量化抗生素使用时间窗（30 天 vs 60 天）对 OS 的影响。该材料提供了癌种特异性证据和临床实践中的时间敏感性数据，适合讨论宿主生理状态与微生物组的交互作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0289\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome Landscape and Association with Response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Advanced Solid Tumors: A SCRUM-Japan MONSTAR-SCREEN Study\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在跨癌种队列中发现α多样性与疗效无整体关联，但粪便口腔细菌富集（尤其 PPI 使用者）与 PFS 缩短显著相关。该材料挑战了通用多样性假说，提出口腔细菌易位作为负面预测因子，适合讨论药物（PPI）介导的菌群改变及其临床意义。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0290\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract A14: Meta-analysis improves identification of microbiome associations with antitumor response in melanoma, lung, and kidney cancer patients treated with checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"通过荟萃分析校正假阳性，确认特定细菌签名与 ICI 响应的关联，并指出α多样性非稳定预测因子。该材料提供了经过统计校正的跨癌种证据，适合用于讨论生物标志物的一致性问题及复合指数优于单一标志物的趋势。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0291\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Role of the intestinal microbiome and microbial-derived metabolites in immune checkpoint blockade immunotherapy of cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"区分抗原依赖与非依赖两大机制路径，列举关键 taxa 和代谢物，并讨论 FMT 和抗生素影响的临床证据。该综述提供了机制分类框架和临床转化现状，适合用于构建理论模型和讨论从分类学到功能分析的范式转变。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0292\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Predictive impact of sarcopenia in solid cancers treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors: a meta‐analysis\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供肌少症降低 ICI 疗效的荟萃分析证据，并提出肌源性细胞因子（IL-15）调节免疫的假说。虽不直接涉及微生物组，但可作为宿主全身状态影响疗效的对比案例，适合讨论多因素（肌肉 - 免疫轴 vs 菌群 - 免疫轴）共同决定预后的复杂性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0293\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota's role in NAFLD- and HBV/HCV-related hepatocellular carcinoma: Mechanisms and therapeutic implications.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"综述 HCC 背景下微生物群通过 LPS-TLR4 信号和胆汁酸失调诱导免疫抑制微环境的机制，提及 SCFA 的抗炎作用。虽未直接针对 ICI，但提供了肝病特异性微生物 - 免疫互作背景，适合讨论基础疾病状态对免疫治疗微环境的潜在修饰。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0294\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The role of the gut microbiome in modulating immunotherapy efficacy in colorectal cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"聚焦结直肠癌，详述 SCFA 抑制 NF-κB、促进 DC 成熟等机制，并总结 FMT、益生菌干预的早期临床结果。该材料提供了癌种特异性的机制深度和干预证据，适合用于讨论消化道肿瘤中微生物组的独特作用及转化策略。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0295\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Checkpoint inhibitor responses can be regulated by the gut microbiota – A systematic review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"系统梳理跨癌种响应/无响应相关的细菌物种列表，指出方法学（测序技术、样本类型）导致的异质性。该材料提供了经过筛选的 taxa 清单和方法学批判，适合用于构建临床关联证据基础及讨论结果不一致的技术原因。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0296\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiota: A key factor affecting and regulating the efficacy of immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提出“微生物 - 宿主信号传导”和“微生物向肿瘤易位”两大机制维度，界定微生物组组成范围。作为概念框架综述，它适合用于引导机制章节的结构化讨论，提示从整体生态到具体分子通路的探索路径，但需结合实证研究填充细节。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome in lung cancer: from pathogenesis to precision therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch5_Interventions\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"详述肠 - 肺轴中微生物代谢物（SCFA）、免疫细胞启动及细菌易位机制，总结肺癌特异性菌群标志物及干预策略。该材料提供了器官特异性轴线的深度解析，适合用于讨论远端器官（肺）受肠道菌群调节的独特机制及精准治疗前景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0298\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbial signatures and immunotherapy outcomes in NSCLC and melanoma: a systematic review and meta-analysis\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"提供 NSCLC 和黑色素瘤中微生物特征（多样性、特定菌属）与生存/响应改善的定量荟萃证据，并提出功能趋同假说。该材料提供了高等级关联证据和机制假设，适合用于确立核心临床结论及引导未来功能研究方向。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0299\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Impact of Periodontal Host-Modulation Therapies on Oral–Gut Microbiome Axis in Periodontitis Patients with Hematological Diseases: A Narrative Review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4_Context\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦血液病，但详述口 - 肠轴中牙周病原体易位致全身炎症的机制，提示口腔健康对免疫稳态的影响。可作为背景材料讨论口 - 肠轴在实体瘤中的潜在作用，特别是口腔菌群失调作为系统性炎症来源的可能性，但需谨慎外推至 ICI 疗效。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0300\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"[Intestinal microbiom modulates the response to antitumor immunotherapy].\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2_Clinical\",\n        \"Ch3_Mechanisms\",\n        \"Ch6_Challenges\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"列举黑色素瘤、肺癌中响应者相关菌群（粪杆菌、阿克曼氏菌）及抗生素负面影响，概述 T 细胞激活和代谢物介导机制。作为早期综述，它提供了基础 taxa 列表和机制框架，同时强调标志物不一致性，适合用于历史脉络梳理和方法学反思。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to route a batch of 60 sources (P0241-P0300) to the chapters of a shared outline for a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\n\nI need to:\n1. Read each source's B_review_planning card carefully\n2. Determine which chapter(s) each source belongs to based on its actual content, research type, object, conditions, and depth\n3. Write specific_usable_material in Chinese (80-150 characters) explaining what specific facts or comparison angles are usable and their purpose in the review\n4. Not force irrelevant sources into chapters\n5. Return JSON only with source_routes array\n\nLet me analyze each source:\n\n**P0241**: H. pylori infection in gastric cancer patients treated with ICIs - Clinical association study\n- Chapter: Ch2_Clinical (clinical association evidence), Ch4_Context (specific pathogen effect)\n- Material: Active H. pylori infection associated with lower DCR (47.1% vs 72.1%) and shorter survival in advanced gastric cancer ICI patients\n\n**P0242**: PD-L2/RGMb mechanism - Mouse model with mechanistic evidence\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (molecular mechanism), Ch5_Interventions (overcoming resistance strategy)\n- Material: Microbiome downregulates PD-L2 on DCs, reducing PD-L2/RGMb inhibitory interaction on CD8+ T cells; C. cateniformis identified\n\n**P0243**: Gut microbiota and ICI response association - Small observational study (N=50)\n- Chapter: Ch2_Clinical (clinical association), Ch3_Mechanisms (immune phenotype correlation)\n- Material: Alpha-diversity associated with clinical benefit; high diversity linked to reduced Treg and inflammatory cytokines\n\n\n- Material: MRx0518 live biotherapeutic shows immune gene expression changes in tumor tissue pre-surgery; early clinical safety data available\n\n**P0245**: ICB resistance in lung cancer review - Narrative review\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (resistance mechanisms framework), Ch4_Context (lung cancer specific)\n- Material: Microbiome positioned as microenvironment factor cooperating with other factors to promote immunosuppression\n\n**P0246**: PPIs use and ICI outcomes in NSCLC - Large observational study\n- Chapter: Ch2_Clinical (clinical association), Ch4_Context (medication effect)\n- Material: PPIs associated with reduced 5-year survival (37.2% vs 28.3%) and shorter median survival (~214 days) in NSCLC patients on ICIs\n\n; proposed microbiome-mediated mechanisms\n\n**P0247**: Microbiome in antitumor immunity review 2025 - Full text review\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (mechanism framework), Ch6_Challenges (methodological challenges)\n- Material: Three mediator mechanisms (metabolites, antigens, local colonization); methodological discussion on 16S limitations, need for multi-omics\n\n**P0248**: Microbiome in hematological malignancies review - NOT solid tumors\n- Chapter: Potentially Ch3_Mechanisms (general mechanisms), but primarily hematological\n- Material: General mechanisms (SCFAs, T-cell regulation) but explicitly focused on hematological cancers - limited direct applicability to solid tumors\n\n**P0249**: Black raspberry dietary intervention - Abstract only, preliminary\n- Chapter: Ch5_Interventions (dietary intervention), Ch6_Challenges (methodological limitations)\n- Material: Human microbiome avatar model showed tumor suppression in mice; human A. muciniphila change not significant - shows complexity of diet-microbiome-ICI axis\n\n**P0250**: Melanoma microbiome and anti-PD-1 review - Full text review\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (mechanism details), Ch5_Interventions (intervention strategies)\n- Material: Detailed mechanism map including specific species, metabolites, immune cell interactions; FMT, diet, probiotics evidence summary\n\n**P0251**: Microbial mechanisms to improve ICB responsiveness review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (molecular mechanisms), Ch5_Interventions (intervention strategies)\n- Material: Specific effector molecules (cdAMP, inosine, muropeptides) and host receptors; engineered probiotic design concepts\n\n**P0252**: Diet and probiotics influence on ICI response review - Abstract only\n- Chapter: Ch5_Interventions (dietary/probiotic interventions), Ch4_Context (modifiable factors)\n- Material: Categorizes dietary factors (Mediterranean, vegan, omega-3, polyphenols) and their general direction of effect on ICI response\n\n**P0253**: Melanoma microbiome and immunotherapy review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch2_Clinical (clinical evidence), Ch3_Mechanisms (mechanism clues), Ch5_Interventions (FMT evidence)\n- Material: Specific taxa lists (Bifidobacterium, Faecalibacterium vs Ruminococcus obeum); FMT restores immune sensitivity evidence\n\n**P0254**: Obesity, cancer, ICI response review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch4_Context (host factors - obesity), Ch3_Mechanisms (metabolic/immune pathways)\n- Material: Obesity paradox clinical evidence; microbiota as mechanistic bridge (SCFAs, leptin, inflammation); discordant microbial signals\n\n**P0255**: Chinese review on microbiome and ICIs - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch2_Clinical (taxa-ICI associations), Ch3_Mechanisms (mechanisms), Ch5_Interventions (clinical trials)\n- Material: Different ICI types (PD-1 vs CTLA-4 vs CD47) corresponding taxa lists; mechanism pathways (STING, inosine, Th1); clinical trial status\n\n**P0256**: TNBC ICI utilization - Abstract only, NO microbiome content\n- Chapter: Not directly relevant (no microbiome data)\n- Material: Establishes clinical baseline of ICI efficacy in TNBC but does not address microbiome\n\n**P0257**: Pancreatic cancer microbiome and immunotherapy review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (cell mechanisms, metabolites), Ch5_Interventions (intervention attempts), Ch4_Context (tumor type specificity)\n- Material: PDAC-specific evidence; SCFAs, TMAO, bile acid mechanisms; Vancomycin+Nivolumab trial negative result\n\n**P0258**: Gut microbiota effect on ICI review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (three main mechanisms), Ch2_Clinical (taxa associations), Ch6_Challenges (controversies)\n- Material: Three mechanisms (molecular mimicry, DC activation, metabolites); specific taxa lists; controversies and individual variability\n\n**P0259**: Cutaneous toxicities observational study - NO microbiome content\n- Chapter: Ch4_Context (toxicity context), but limited relevance\n- Material: Grade 3/4 skin toxicity baseline (1.7%); treatment discontinuation rates - provides safety context but no microbiome mechanism\n\n**P0260**: Immunotoxicity review 2025 - Full text, focus on toxicity NOT efficacy\n- Chapter: Ch4_Context (toxicity-efficacy tradeoff), limited Ch2_Clinical\n- Material: Akkermansia dual effect (enhances survival but increases irAE risk); Th17 regulation - primarily toxicity focused\n\n**P0261**: Facts and Hopes for Gut Microbiota Interventions review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (three mechanistic categories), Ch5_Interventions (FMT, consortia trials), Ch6_Challenges (biomarker inconsistency)\n- Material: Three mechanisms (T-cell stimulation, mimicry, metabolites); early FMT/consortia trial results; cohort heterogeneity challenges\n\n**P0262**: Bacterial microbiome in cancer treatment review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (three mechanism framework), Ch2_Clinical (taxa lists), Ch5_Interventions (FMT, probiotics)\n- Material: Three mechanisms (metabolism, immune response, translocation); specific taxa (Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium); intervention examples\n\n**P0263**: Advanced urothelial carcinoma ICI review - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch4_Context (concomitant medications), Ch5_Interventions (probiotic trials)\n- Material: Antibiotics, PPIs, corticosteroids negative impact via microbiome; CBM588 probiotic preliminary RCT data\n\n**P0264**: Systematic evaluation of immune regulation review 2017 - Full text\n- Chapter: Ch3_Mechanisms (general framework), Ch6_Challenges (methodological standardization)\n- Material: Microbiome as necessary condition for ICI efficacy; sample collection, sequencing, analysis standardization discussion\n\n**P0265**: Immuno-oncology biomarkers challenge review 2017 - Structured partial",
